        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2dd4662c-d3ee-5644-94e0-82b87b9b7370",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michaël Llodra, Juan Martín del Potro, Novak Djokovic, Tomáš Berdych, Robin Söderling, Jo-Wilfried Tsonga, Nikolay Davydenko, Janko Tipsarević, John Isner, Gaël Monfils\n- Events: 2009 ABN AMRO World Tennis Tournament – Singles\n- Organizations: Association of Tennis Professionals\n- Topics: men's singles rankings, doubles success, singles titles\n\nFacts:\n- Juan Martín del Potro was born on 23 September 1988.\n- Michaël Llodra won the singles title before the 2009 ABN AMRO World Tennis Tournament and entered the 2009 event as the defending champion.\n- At the 2009 ABN AMRO World Tennis Tournament – Singles, Gaël Monfils defeated Michaël Llodra in the second round.\n- Michaël Llodra was a successful doubles player who won three Grand Slam championships and an Olympic silver medal.\n- Michaël Llodra also had singles success, winning five career titles.\n- Michaël Llodra recorded singles victories over Novak Djokovic, Juan Martín del Potro, Tomáš Berdych, Robin Söderling, Jo-Wilfried Tsonga, Nikolay Davydenko, Janko Tipsarević, and John Isner.\n- Juan Martín del Potro was also known as Delpo.\n- Juan Martín del Potro was an Argentinian professional tennis player.\n- Juan Martín del Potro was ranked world No. 24 in men's singles by the Association of Tennis Professionals.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
